   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to ambulance services which\nprovide transportation by aircraft; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2021\namending the public health law relating to availability of air transport\nambulance service providers to store and distribute blood, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 4085-A and A. 2561-B, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7839",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7839-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 45,
       "fullName": "Dan Stec",
       "imgName": "674_dan_stec.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1490,
       "sessionMemberId": 1845,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "STEC"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3003-b, Pub Health L; amd §2, Chap of 2021 (as proposed in S.4085-A & A.2561-B)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7839\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to ambulance services\nwhich provide transportation by aircraft; and to amend a chapter of the\nlaws of 2021 amending the public health law relating to availability of\nair transport ambulance service providers to store and distribute blood,\nas proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 4085-A and A. 2561-B, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2021,\nc.779.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThe underlying chapter authorizes air transport ambulance service\nproviders to store and distribute blood, distribute blood and blood\nproducts, and initiate and administer transfusions while providing air\ntransport services. This chapter amendment changes \"air transport ambu-\nlance service providers\" to \"ambulance service that provides transporta-\ntion by aircraft.\" Adds the definition of \"air transport services\" to\nmean \"emergency medical care and the transportation of sick or injured\npersons by aircraft to, from, or between general hospitals or other\nhealth care facilities. Adds language to state that qualified personnel\nmay initiate and administer transfusions while providing emergency and\nnon-emergency medical care within the aircraft. Eliminates language to\nchange the regulatory body that will oversee this new service (from the\nCouncil on Human Blood and Transfusion Services to the State Emergency\nMedical Services Council) and authorizes the EMS Council to promulgate\nregulations. Adds a requirement for providers to ensure compliance with\nlaws and regulations and provide DOH with a notice of intent to offer\nthese services at least 60 days before starting the services. It also\nchanges the effective date of the underlying chapter to 90 days.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter to\nensure air transport ambulance service providers store and administer\nblood products following the State's safety standards and regulations.\nAlso, it is crucial for the ambulance service provider to provide prior\nnotification to the Department of Health (DOH) of its intent to store\nand distribute blood so DOH can monitor compliance.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 779 of the Laws of 2021. S.4085-A and\nA.2561-B both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in May 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; .provided, however, that section\none of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the same\nmanner as a chapter of the laws of 2021 amending the public health law\nrelating to availability of air transport ambulance service providers to\nstore and distribute blood, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS.4085-A and A.2561-B, takes effect.\n",
